  "aiOverview": {
    "content": "In April 2023, actress Olivia Munn, 43, was diagnosed with stage 1 luminal B bilateral breast cancer, an aggressive form, despite a clean mammogram and negative genetic testing. She underwent a double mastectomy and several subsequent surgeries, including a hysterectomy. A high-risk assessment score prompted by her doctor saved her life. Key Details of Olivia Munn's Breast Cancer Journey Diagnosis: Munn was diagnosed with fast-growing, bilateral cancer (cancer in both breasts) after her OB/GYN used the Tyrer-Cuzick Risk Assessment Calculator and determined she had a 37% chance of developing breast cancer. Initial Symptoms & Tests: She had no family history of breast cancer and a normal mammogram just two months prior to her diagnosis. Treatment: She underwent four surgeries over 10 months, including a double mastectomy, a lymph node dissection, and a nipple delay procedure. She also underwent a hysterectomy and oophorectomy to stop cancer-feeding hormones. Raising Awareness: Munn has become a vocal advocate for women to ask their doctors to calculate their Breast Cancer Risk Assessment Tool (.gov) score. Family Impact: Following her diagnosis, her mother, Kim, also tested positive for breast cancer. Current Status: Munn is taking hormone suppression therapy to prevent recurrence. Prevent Cancer Foundation notes her story caused a massive surge in people using online risk assessment tools.",
